Garner Health is proud to be an Equal Employment Opportunity employer and values diversity in the workplace. We do not discriminate based upon race, religion, color, national origin, sex (including pregnancy, childbirth, reproductive health decisions, or related medical conditions), sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, age, status as a protected veteran, status as an individual with a disability, genetic information, political views or activity, or other applicable legally protected characteristics.
&lt;p&gt;Garner Health is committed to providing accommodations for qualified individuals with disabilities in our recruiting process. If you need assistance or an accommodation due to a disability, you may contact us at &lt;a href=&quot;mailto:talent@getgarner.com&quot;&gt;talent@garnerhealth.com&lt;/a&gt;.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Snorkel&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Snorkel AI is the frontier AI data lab, helping teams build the data and environments behind high-performing frontier and agentic AI. We combine technology with research-driven AI data development to create datasets, benchmarks, evals, and custom solutions for real-world AI systems. Founded out of the Stanford AI Lab in 2019, Snorkel works with leading AI labs and enterprises to move from better data to better outcomes.&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Excited to help us redefine how AI is built? Apply to be the newest Snorkeler!&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Role:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for a Technical Product Manager to own the roadmap and execution across Snorkel AI&#39;s Infrastructure organization, spanning three engineering pods: Core Services, Developer Experience, and Security. This is not a customer-facing product role, you will be the PM for internal platforms, data infrastructure, and security systems that the rest of engineering and the business depend on. You will be the single point of coordination across a broad surface area that currently lacks dedicated product leadership.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You Will Do:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Infrastructure org owns the data platform, event systems, observability, developer tooling, release pipelines, and the full security stack. The engineering leadership and pod leads are very technical but the org needs a PM who can translate business and compliance requirements into prioritized infrastructure investments, manage dependencies across pods and partner teams, and hold the line on scope and delivery timelines. Today, prioritization decisions are made ad hoc by engineering leads who are also deep in technical execution. This role gives the org a dedicated owner for roadmap clarity, stakeholder alignment, and cross-pod coordination.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Business context and infrastructure strategy:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop a deep understanding of Snorkel AI&#39;s business, how the datasets are sold, and how should the platform be deployed, and scaled to support customers across AI labs, enterprise and federal and use that context to work closely with engineering leaders and product PMs to translate business scaling, security and functional needs into deployment patterns, and go-to-market requirements into concrete, prioritized projects for the Infrastructure org. Without this, infrastructure roadmaps become technically interesting but disconnected from what actually moves the business forward.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Roadmap and prioritization across all three pods:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with engineering leads to define quarterly roadmaps for Core Services (data platform, metrics platform, event systems, observability, fraud detection, infrastructure cost management, platform customization infrastructure, SDS project infrastructure), Developer Experience (CI/CD, release pipelines, dev systems, AI dev tooling), and Security (Auth0 migration, AuthN/AuthZ, cloud security, encryption).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Make trade-off decisions when pods compete for shared resources or when new asks land mid-quarter. The org carries significant surface area relative to headcount. Your job is to ensure the team is working on the highest-leverage problems, not just the loudest requests.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Stakeholder management and requirements gathering:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be the interface between the Infrastructure org and its consumers: product engineering teams who depend on Dataset APIs, Platform APIs, and Packaging APIs; the data science and analytics teams who depend on Cascade and the transformation layer; GTM and customer success teams who surface compliance and security requirements from enterprise and federal customers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translate customer compliance requirements (SOC 2, FedRAMP, GDPR) into concrete security and data governance work items with clear acceptance criteria.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Adoption and internal evangelism:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proactively engage product PMs and engineering leads to ensure teams are leveraging infrastructure services, SDKs, and shared libraries (unified data access, event bus, security SDKs, CI/CD tooling) rather than building one-off solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track adoption metrics, SDK integration coverage, service onboarding rates, migration completions, and identify teams that are lagging or working around infrastructure offerings. Close the loop by either driving adoption or feeding unmet requirements back into the roadmap.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The Infrastructure org&#39;s impact is only as real as its adoption. You own the push to make sure the work doesn&#39;t just ship, it lands.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Cross-pod coordination on foundational initiatives:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive initiatives that span multiple pods, such as the unified data access library (which touches Core Services for the library itself, Security for auth/RBAC/encryption enforcement, and Developer Experience for SDK distribution and testing tooling).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate the event bus rollout across services, ensuring schema governance, consumer onboarding, and observability are sequenced correctly.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the Auth0 migration program as a cross-functional deliverable that touches Security, Core Services, and every API team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Metrics, reporting, and visibility:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define and track key metrics across pods: data platform query latency, event bus propagation latency, CI pipeline duration, release rollback rate, security finding remediation time, encryption coverage, infrastructure cost per workload.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide regular reporting to VP-level leadership on infrastructure org health, delivery status, and risk areas.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain a clear view of staffing gaps and make the case for headcount investments backed by roadmap impact.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Infrastructure cost and efficiency:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Core Services on infrastructure cost visibility, attribution, and optimization. Own the narrative around infrastructure spend not just tracking it, but driving decisions on reserved capacity, right-sizing, and cost allocation by team and product.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own inference cost management as a cross-functional concern that touches both infrastructure and product economics.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum Qualifications:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;7+ years of product management experience, with at least 2 years in infrastructure, platform, or developer tools PM roles. You have shipped internal platforms or infrastructure products, not just customer-facing features.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong technical fluency. You don&#39;t need to write Terraform modules, but you need to understand what an event bus is, why CDC lag matters, what RBAC enforcement means at the data layer, and why audit logs shouldn&#39;t live in the production database. You can hold your own in architecture discussions and push back on technical proposals with substance, not just process.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with compliance and security programs. You have worked on SOC 2, FedRAMP, or similar compliance frameworks and understand how to translate audit requirements into engineering work items. You know the difference between checking a box and actually being secure.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort with ambiguity and breadth. This role covers platform infrastructure, data infrastructure, developer tooling, and security, three domains that each could be a full-time PM role at a larger company. You are comfortable context-switching, prioritizing ruthlessly, and saying no to work that doesn&#39;t clear the bar.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with small, high-leverage engineering teams.You understand that with small teams, every quarter&#39;s roadmap is a zero-sum game, and your job is to make sure the bets are right.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Fluency with AI-assisted workflows is a plus.&lt;/strong&gt; The org treats AI tooling (Claude Code, Cursor) as a baseline expectation for engineers; a PM who understands and can evaluate these tools&#39; impact on developer productivity will be more effective in this role.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred Qualifications:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;7+ years of experience as a Product Manager, including 3+ years focused on ML/AI products, MLOps, Platform infrastructure or data systems products.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with agent-based systems, generative AI, reinforcement learning, self-improving systems, or automated workforce/task routing platforms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with LLMs, LLM Evaluations, human-in-the-loop systems, and synthetic data generation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Background in Computer Science, Security or related technical field.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to lead large, cross-team initiatives without formal authority.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Actual compensation will be determined based on factors including skills, qualifications, experience, and geographic location.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Salary range(s) for this role&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$260,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$300,000 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Be Your Best at Snorkel&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Joining Snorkel AI means becoming part of a company that has market proven solutions, robust funding, and is scaling rapidly—offering a unique combination of stability and the excitement of high growth. As a member of our team, you’ll have meaningful opportunities to shape priorities and initiatives, influence key strategic decisions, and directly impact our ongoing success. Whether you’re looking to deepen your technical expertise, explore leadership opportunities, or learn new skills across multiple functions, you’re fully supported in building your career in an environment designed for growth, learning, and shared success.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Snorkel AI is proud to be an Equal Employment Opportunity employer and is committed to building a team that represents a variety of backgrounds, perspectives, and skills. Snorkel AI embraces diversity and provides equal employment opportunities to all employees and applicants for employment. Snorkel AI prohibits discrimination and harassment of any type on the basis of race, color, religion, age, sex, national origin, disability status, genetics, protected veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, or any other characteristic protected by federal, state, or local law. All employment is decided on the basis of qualifications, performance, merit, and business need.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;We will ensure that individuals with disabilities are provided reasonable accommodation to participate in the job application or interview process, to perform essential job functions, and to receive other benefits and privileges of employment. Please contact us to request accommodation.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll be part of&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Garner is on a mission to transform the U.S. healthcare system — and we’re the only proven player doing exactly that. We partner with employers to redesign how healthcare works: applying 550+ proprietary clinical metrics across 80+ specialties to a dataset of 320M+ patients to identify the best-performing doctors, then using compelling incentives to steer members to the care that helps them get healthier, faster.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The result is a rare “win win” — better care and lower costs for both members and employers. In just five years, our work has helped over 2.5 million people access higher-quality care and saved $1B in healthcare costs. We recently raised our Series E and have doubled five years running. If you&#39;ve ever wanted your work to solve a problem that touches every person in this country, this is the opportunity to do exactly that. You&#39;d be joining a team fundamentally reimagining healthcare in the U.S. — and using AI to scale that impact further and faster than anyone else can.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;We are seeking an exceptional &lt;strong&gt;Senior Marketing Analytics Manager &lt;/strong&gt;to be embedded in&lt;strong&gt; Growth Marketing&lt;/strong&gt;, the team at Garner that owns B2C member activation &amp;amp; engagement. You will report directly to the &lt;strong&gt;Director of Marketing Operations&lt;/strong&gt; and serve as the dedicated data &amp;amp; analytics partner for our&lt;strong&gt; Growth Marketing &lt;/strong&gt;team.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Growth Marketing is responsible for getting employees to sign up and use their Garner benefit — through email, SMS, direct mail, in-app, in-office materials, and employer-led communication channels. We&#39;re looking for an &lt;strong&gt;exceptional, AI-native data &amp;amp; analytics manager &lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;to own how member activation and engagement are operationalized and measured across channels. You&#39;ll own the &lt;strong&gt;audience targeting &amp;amp; segmentation&lt;/strong&gt; (SQL queries in Snowflake for our email / sms / direct mail targeting, partnering closely with Engineering) and build the &lt;strong&gt;Business Intelligence layer &lt;/strong&gt;that powers our member engagement campaigns, ranging from cross-system data pipelines, attribution modeling, experimentation frameworks, and funnel &amp;amp; lifecycle analysis through core reporting and dashboards. You&#39;ll define the metrics behind member growth and ensure those definitions hold consistently across systems. This is a high-impact role at the heart of our growth engine — helping us engage more members, deliver a first-class member experience, and improve health outcomes at scale.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Where you will work:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role will be based in our New York City office (in the Financial District). You must be willing to work in the office 3 days per week on Tuesday, Wednesday and Thursday.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you will do:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Targeting &amp;amp; segmentation (campaign operations): &lt;/strong&gt;Own the audience targeting, segmentation (SQL queries of Snowflake data tables to be built into our Iterable system), and personalization data behind our email, SMS, and direct mail campaigns. Partner with Engineering to troubleshoot upstream Data issues that affect our marketing campaigns, as well as enhance and automate the data mechanics and pipelines so the program can scale.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Analytics &amp;amp; Reporting:&lt;/strong&gt; Own how member activation and engagement are measured end-to-end (e.g., Looker dashboards). Define, build, and maintain the KPIs, metric definitions, performance reports, and dashboards Growth Marketing runs on — funnel and lifecycle metrics, email/SMS campaign activity, channel efficiency, operational health, and KPI target setting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Product &amp;amp; engagement analytics:&lt;/strong&gt; Bridge marketing activity to member behavior in the Garner app so the team can optimize communications over time.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Experimentation: &lt;/strong&gt;Develop and execute on the Growth Marketing team’s A/B testing program and performance reporting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Data governance:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;Build our data foundation alongside Data Management &amp;amp; Engineering, Reporting &amp;amp; Business Intelligence, Growth Product to ensure our data is analysis-ready and trustworthy. Build workflows, documentation, QA practices, and tooling that ensure our metrics are standardized across systems and campaigns.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Systems &amp;amp; technology stack:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;Uplevel our data sophistication by designing and building at the systems level, leveraging AI in order to maximize scale and leverage.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you will bring to the team:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;4–6+ years in marketing &amp;amp; growth &amp;amp; analytics, business intelligence, growth analytics, marketing analytics, or a similar data-centric role.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Growth &amp;amp; marketing, B2C, B2B2C, and Product-led Growth subject matter expertise preferred but not required (e.g., customer funnel analytics, cohort and retention curves, channel attribution, lifecycle email/SMS/direct mail performance, targeting/segmentation, personalization)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Expertise in the modern data stack&lt;/strong&gt;. &lt;strong&gt;Hands-on proficiency with Snowflake, SQL, Python, and visualization tools&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp; (e.g., Looker, Tableau, Power BI, or similar). Experience with ESP/CRM event data (Iterable, Braze, Salesforce Marketing Cloud, Klaviyo, or similar) is a strong plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Experience in experimentation &amp;amp; reporting&lt;/strong&gt;. Familiarity with A/B and incrementality test design, statistics, measurement, and optimization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Analytical rigor and problem framing&lt;/strong&gt;. You turn a vague business question into the right analysis, define a defensible metric, and state your assumptions rather than jumping to a chart. You’re a strong communicator who’s comfortable using insight to drive decisions for a marketing audience and executives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;AI fluency&lt;/strong&gt;. Comfort with and excitement about harnessing AI agents to build analyses, design dashboards, and validate results.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Self-starter approach&lt;/strong&gt; with the ability to “roll up your sleeves” and juggle multiple priorities &amp;amp; deadlines, doing whatever is necessary to ensure company success. You thrive in a &lt;strong&gt;fast-paced, dynamic &lt;/strong&gt;startup environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A desire to be a part of a high-performing, mission-driven team&lt;/strong&gt; that operates with intense urgency, a strong sense of individual accountability, and a commitment to authentic feedback.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;Please note: we are unable to sponsor or take over sponsorship of an employment visa at this time.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you&#39;ll get here:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll work on problems that matter, at a company working to change healthcare at scale. You’ll work at the intersection of AI and systemic healthcare reform, where the problems we solve are as interesting and compelling as the mission.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Garner, you’ll take on real, ambitious problems with real ownership and autonomy, alongside exceptional, principles-based people who genuinely want you to win. It’s demanding by design. You’ll be challenged to stretch beyond what you thought possible and receive consistent coaching to help you grow and do the best work of your career. This isn&#39;t the right fit for everyone, and that&#39;s intentional. The people here are driven by what&#39;s at stake for real people, and that&#39;s what gives our intensity its purpose.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Compensation Transparency:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The target salary range for this position is $150,000 - $175,000. Individual compensation for this role will depend on various factors, including qualifications, skills, and applicable laws. In addition to base compensation, this role is eligible to participate in our equity incentive and competitive benefits plans, including but not limited to: flexible PTO, Medical/Dental/Vision plan options, 401(k) with company match, flexible spending accounts, Teladoc Health and more.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;div&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Fraud and Security Notice:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Please be aware of recent job scam attempts. Our recruiters use &lt;a href=&quot;http://getgarner.com/&quot;&gt;getgarner.com&lt;/a&gt; and &lt;a href=&quot;garnerhealth.com&quot;&gt;garnerhealth.com&lt;/a&gt; email domains exclusively. If you have been contacted by someone claiming to be a Garner recruiter or a hiring manager from a different domain about a potential job, please report it to law enforcement &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.ic3.gov/Home/ComplaintChoice&quot;&gt;here&lt;/a&gt; and to &lt;a href=&quot;mailto:candidateprotection@getgarner.com&quot;&gt;candidateprotection@garnerhealth.com&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Equal Employment Opportunity:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
Garner Health is proud to be an Equal Employment Opportunity employer and values diversity in the workplace. We do not discriminate based upon race, religion, color, national origin, sex (including pregnancy, childbirth, reproductive health decisions, or related medical conditions), sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, age, status as a protected veteran, status as an individual with a disability, genetic information, political views or activity, or other applicable legally protected characteristics.
&lt;p&gt;Garner Health is committed to providing accommodations for qualified individuals with disabilities in our recruiting process. If you need assistance or an accommodation due to a disability, you may contact us at &lt;a href=&quot;mailto:talent@getgarner.com&quot;&gt;talent@garnerhealth.com&lt;/a&gt;.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Snorkel&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Snorkel AI is the frontier AI data lab, helping teams build the data and environments behind high-performing frontier and agentic AI. We combine technology with research-driven AI data development to create datasets, benchmarks, evals, and custom solutions for real-world AI systems. Founded out of the Stanford AI Lab in 2019, Snorkel works with leading AI labs and enterprises to move from better data to better outcomes.&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Excited to help us redefine how AI is built? Apply to be the newest Snorkeler!&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Snorkel AI is looking for a Director of Talent Acquisition Operations &amp;amp; Insights to build and lead the systems, processes, tools, metrics, and operational infrastructure that power our recruiting organization. This leader will own the design and execution of a modern TA operations function that enables Snorkel AI to scale hiring with speed, quality, consistency, and data-driven decision-making.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a builder role for someone who has stood up TA operations in a hyper-growth technical startup environment. You should be equally comfortable designing the strategy, implementing the systems, improving process, building reporting, leading recruiting coordination, and partnering with recruiting and business leaders to improve how hiring gets done.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for someone who brings strong operational discipline, deep knowledge of recruiting systems and workflows, and a forward-looking perspective on how AI can modernize talent acquisition.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You’ll Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and lead the TA operations function for Snorkel AI, including recruiting systems, tools, workflows, reporting, process, and coordination.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the recruiting tech stack, including ATS configuration, integrations, automation, data quality, vendor management, and tool optimization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Modernize TA operations through better systems, scalable processes, automation, and thoughtful use of AI.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead recruiting coordination, ensuring a high-quality, efficient, and consistent candidate and hiring manager experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and improve end-to-end recruiting processes across intake, approvals, job posting, sourcing workflows, interview scheduling, feedback collection, offers, onboarding handoffs, and reporting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and maintain TA metrics, dashboards, insights and reporting for recruiting leadership, hiring managers, and company leadership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use data to identify process gaps, pipeline bottlenecks, operational risks, interviewer capacity issues, and opportunities for improvement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with recruiting leaders, People Operations, Finance, Legal, IT, and business stakeholders to ensure TA processes are scalable, compliant, and aligned with company priorities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create governance and documentation for recruiting operations, including process guides, system standards, SLAs, data definitions, and reporting cadences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Evaluate and implement AI-enabled recruiting tools and workflows that improve recruiter productivity, candidate experience, scheduling efficiency, sourcing support, and decision quality.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build operational rhythms for headcount planning, recruiting capacity planning, funnel reviews, and hiring progress reporting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure data integrity across recruiting systems so leaders can make confident decisions based on accurate information.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We’re Looking For&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building or leading TA operations in a hyper-growth technical startup environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep experience owning recruiting systems, tools, processes, reporting, and operational infrastructure.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of ATS architecture, recruiting workflows, system integrations, data hygiene, and recruiting analytics.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading recruiting coordination or designing scheduling operations at scale.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical skills, with experience building dashboards, reporting frameworks, and metrics that drive business decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience using data to improve recruiting productivity, funnel conversion, hiring speed, candidate experience, and operational accountability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A track record of modernizing TA operations through process improvement, automation, tooling, or AI-enabled workflows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong project management skills, with the ability to manage cross-functional initiatives from design through implementation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent stakeholder management skills across Recruiting, People, Finance, Legal, IT, and business leadership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort operating in fast-changing environments where systems and processes need to be built, improved, and scaled quickly.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;This role is hybrid (&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;3 days/week in office)&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt; in our San Francisco or New York city office&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The compensation range for this role is between $170,000 and $300,000. Our compensation ranges are determined by role, level, and location. Within the range, individual pay is determined by work location and additional factors, including job-related skills, experience, and relevant education or training.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;#LI - GM&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Actual compensation will be determined based on factors including skills, qualifications, experience, and geographic location.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Salary range(s) for this role&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$170,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$300,000 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Be Your Best at Snorkel&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Joining Snorkel AI means becoming part of a company that has market proven solutions, robust funding, and is scaling rapidly—offering a unique combination of stability and the excitement of high growth. As a member of our team, you’ll have meaningful opportunities to shape priorities and initiatives, influence key strategic decisions, and directly impact our ongoing success. Whether you’re looking to deepen your technical expertise, explore leadership opportunities, or learn new skills across multiple functions, you’re fully supported in building your career in an environment designed for growth, learning, and shared success.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Snorkel AI is proud to be an Equal Employment Opportunity employer and is committed to building a team that represents a variety of backgrounds, perspectives, and skills. Snorkel AI embraces diversity and provides equal employment opportunities to all employees and applicants for employment. Snorkel AI prohibits discrimination and harassment of any type on the basis of race, color, religion, age, sex, national origin, disability status, genetics, protected veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, or any other characteristic protected by federal, state, or local law. All employment is decided on the basis of qualifications, performance, merit, and business need.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;We will ensure that individuals with disabilities are provided reasonable accommodation to participate in the job application or interview process, to perform essential job functions, and to receive other benefits and privileges of employment. Please contact us to request accommodation.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll be part of&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Garner is on a mission to transform the U.S. healthcare system — and we’re the only proven player doing exactly that. We partner with employers to redesign how healthcare works: applying 550+ proprietary clinical metrics across 80+ specialties to a dataset of 320M+ patients to identify the best-performing doctors, then using compelling incentives to steer members to the care that helps them get healthier, faster.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The result is a rare “win win” — better care and lower costs for both members and employers. In just five years, our work has helped over 2.5 million people access higher-quality care and saved $1B in healthcare costs. We recently raised our Series E and have doubled five years running. If you&#39;ve ever wanted your work to solve a problem that touches every person in this country, this is the opportunity to do exactly that. You&#39;d be joining a team fundamentally reimagining healthcare in the U.S. — and using AI to scale that impact further and faster than anyone else can.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the role:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are seeking an execution-focused and visionary Data Engineering Manager to lead our Data Platform Team. In this critical role, you will manage a team of talented engineers dedicated to building the common, reusable abstractions and high-throughput data infrastructure that power Garner’s internal and external applications. You will champion an AI-native development philosophy and scale our data pipeline capabilities, ensuring our systems seamlessly support the heavy computational demands of our next phase of company-wide growth.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Where you will work:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role will be based in our New York City office (in the Financial District). You must be willing to work in the office 3 days per week on Tuesday, Wednesday and Thursday.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you will do:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead and manage the Data Platform Engineering team, owning the end-to-end design, implementation, and operational excellence of systems that process complex healthcare data&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide high-quality technical contributions and architectural guidance, establishing robust standards for data modeling, processing, and system maintainability&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and optimize common data abstractions, pipelines, and frameworks designed for high scalability, ensuring our platform keeps pace with exponential enterprise data growth&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translate complex, ambiguous business and data requirements into well-scoped, accurately estimated, and composable architectural pieces&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Foster and drive an AI-native engineering culture within the team, integrating cutting-edge AI tools and integrations to enhance development workflows and automate data operations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage and grow stakeholder relationships across Engineering and Product, aligning team priorities with departmental OKRs and broader business goals&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mentor, coach, and guide your team members, conducting detailed design reviews and managing robust Root Cause Analyses (RCA) to continuously elevate technical rigor&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The ideal candidate has:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of hands-on engineering experience, with a focus on Big Data and distributed system and infrastructure&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;2+ years of managing engineering teams, with a track record of building and mentoring high performing teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Expertise with batch data processing frameworks such as Hadoop, Spark, EMR, etc.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with stream processing systems such as Kafka and RedPanda&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency with technologies such as Temporal, Apache iceberg, AWS glue, Spark, DBT, and Soda&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exhibits strong ownership and a proactive mindset, with a proven ability to translate complex business needs into scalable, actionable technical roadmaps&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to operate effectively in dynamic, fast-paced startup environments, with a hands-on approach and a strong commitment to organizational success&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Preference for managing healthcare data standards (e.g. HIPAA, EDI)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A desire to be a part of our mission to improve the U.S. healthcare system&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A desire to be a part of a high-performing, mission-driven team that operates with intense urgency, a strong sense of individual accountability, and a commitment to authentic feedback&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Technologies we use:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Python, Spark, dbt, SnowFlake, Iceberg, Airflow, OpenMetadata, Kubernetes, NATS, AWS, Terraform, Claude Code&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a unique opportunity to join a fast-growing company in a transformative role, helping shape the future of healthcare.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you&#39;ll get here:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll work on problems that matter, at a company working to change healthcare at scale. You’ll work at the intersection of AI and systemic healthcare reform, where the problems we solve are as interesting and compelling as the mission.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Garner, you’ll take on real, ambitious problems with real ownership and autonomy, alongside exceptional, principles-based people who genuinely want you to win. It’s demanding by design. You’ll be challenged to stretch beyond what you thought possible and receive consistent coaching to help you grow and do the best work of your career. This isn&#39;t the right fit for everyone, and that&#39;s intentional. The people here are driven by what&#39;s at stake for real people, and that&#39;s what gives our intensity its purpose.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
