&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are seeking a skilled GTM Engineer to join our team. In this role, you will architect an AI-native tech stack with seamless integrations and build a cohesive, automated engine to drive measurable revenue outcomes. As a builder and systems thinker, you will play a vital role in automating processes, maintaining data integrity, and turning GTM strategy into scalable systems.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Architect the GTM Tech Stack: Build an AI native tech stack with seamless integrations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Centralize Data: Build a cohesive, automated engine that centralizes data in CRM and eventually data warehouse (Salesforce, Hubspot, Snowflake, Clay, Claude Cowork).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own Data Integrity: Build and maintain the data flows, enrichment logic, and sync architecture that keep our systems accurate, deduped, and trustworthy end-to-end.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Turn Strategy into Systems: Partner with leadership to translate GTM strategy into automated playbooks, dynamic scoring models, and signal-based workflows that drive measurable revenue outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead CPQ System Design: Lead system design for Salesforce CPQ, including product catalog architecture, pricing and discount rules, quote templates, and approval workflows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Optimize Conversions: Optimize quote-to-order conversion ensuring accurate data flow into downstream billing and ERP systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Implement Governance: Implement governance on pricing, discounting, and quote approval thresholds to maintain margin and compliance integrity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Improve Deal Velocity: Improve deal velocity by streamlining approvals, leveraging Salesforce CPQ (Revenue Cloud).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Integrate CLM Tools: Integrate CLM (e.g., Ironclad, Conga, or DocuSign CLM) with Salesforce to automate quote-to-contract and contract-to-order workflows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Automate Bottlenecks: Identify repetitive work across the GTM org - account research, CRM hygiene, post-call follow-ups - and replace it with intelligent automation using APIs, webhooks, and AI agents.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience: Have 3–5+ years of experience operating in a Growth, GTM Engineer, or Revenue Operations role. Open to candidates that have a technical background that have worked with a GTM team in other capacities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Systems Thinking: Are a builder and systems thinker: You want to build moonshot ideas, not just toggle settings. You see the GTM stack as an interconnected machine, not a collection of point solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Salesforce Expertise: Have Direct experience with Salesforce — you know the data model, you&#39;ve built on it, and you&#39;re comfortable owning CRM-level changes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;GTM Fluency: Are GTM-fluent: You understand the GTM funnel - not just the data model, but the logic behind every stage. You know what actually converts pipeline because you&#39;ve worked in or alongside GTM teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Quote to Cash Configurations: Strong working knowledge of quoting tool configurations and CLM (pricing rules, product bundles, approval chains).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Execution &amp;amp; Ownership: Constant iteration: Be a Kaizen methodology champion by building, shipping and iterating fast. You thrive in ambiguity, operate with high ownership, and move fast without waiting for perfect requirements. But you know when to slow down and ensure you’re shipping the highest quality work possible.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Technical Capability: Are technically capable: Comfortable working with APIs, webhooks, data integrations and can navigate technical documentation without hand-holding.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior experience at a fast-moving B2B SaaS / AI startup or strong familiarity with the AI tooling ecosystem.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience with Salesforce and Clay, bonus points for building data warehouses.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior quoting tool and CLM implementation experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience designing enrichment and outbounding process and managing complex data sourcing across multiple providers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience centralizing selling signals from multiple data sources into a single location.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have technical familiarity with GTM &amp;amp; automation tools (Salesforce, HubSpot, CPQ, Ironclad, Clay, Gong, Apollo, Clari, APIs, webhooks, etc.).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As our ideal candidate, you will be part engineer, part hacker, with a passion for cybersecurity and a drive to protect our systems from evolving threats.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Together AI&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Together AI, the AI Native Cloud, is purpose-built for AI engineers. AI application developers get high-performance inference that scales reliably, fine-tuning and reinforcement learning for creating frontier-level specialized models, and pre-training at massive scale for fully custom intelligence, all around a marketplace of leading open models that teams can run, adapt, and own. Trusted by Cursor, Decagon, ElevenLabs, Salesforce, and Zoom, Together serves 400+ trillion tokens a month.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Compensation&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We offer competitive compensation, startup equity, health insurance and other competitive benefits. The US base salary range for this full-time position is: $160K-190K + equity + benefits. Our salary ranges are determined by location, level and role. Individual compensation will be determined by experience, skills, and job-related knowledge.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Equal Opportunity&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Together AI is an Equal Opportunity Employer and is proud to offer equal employment opportunity to everyone regardless of race, color, ancestry, religion, sex, national origin, sexual orientation, age, citizenship, marital status, disability, gender identity, veteran status, and more.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Please see our privacy policy at&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.together.ai/privacy&quot;&gt; https://www.together.ai/privacy&lt;/a&gt;.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Snorkel&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Snorkel AI is the frontier AI data lab, helping teams build the data and environments behind high-performing frontier and agentic AI. We combine technology with research-driven AI data development to create datasets, benchmarks, evals, and custom solutions for real-world AI systems. Founded out of the Stanford AI Lab in 2019, Snorkel works with leading AI labs and enterprises to move from better data to better outcomes.&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Excited to help us redefine how AI is built? Apply to be the newest Snorkeler!&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 14pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re hiring a Director of Data Partnerships to lead a new function at Snorkel. You&#39;ll own the supply side of our data partnerships end-to-end: setting the strategy for how we source and procure private data, building the partner / supplier pipeline, structuring agreements, and working with the business to bring it all to life. It is an entrepreneurial, external-facing role that will drive top-of-funnel and convert opportunities into real value. The market for training data partnerships is nascent and rapidly changing - business judgment is key to success in this role. Finally, cross-functional collaboration and a sense of overall ownership are key to ensuring we get value from the partnerships we strike.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role will require hands-on, zero to one work. You&#39;ll be sourcing, qualifying, and negotiating directly. You&#39;ll own the funnel, form a sound but swift view on whether an opportunity is worth pursuing and know which terms to offer and how to negotiate them to close. You&#39;ll carry those relationships forward after signature rather than handing them off. As the function proves out, you&#39;ll build a small but mighty team behind you and shift toward setting direction, standards, and performance expectations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a high-impact role for someone with sharp commercial judgment, meaningful experience in licensing and IP, the creativity and range to operate in a market whose economics and value chain are still being defined - and, critically, hustle. You&#39;ll be a key advisor to leadership on strategy and execution, and you&#39;ll shape how Snorkel acquires data as a matter of company practice. The Business Operations team will help build the internal systems, analytics, and operating cadence alongside you. Success will be measured by the growth of our private data partnerships and the value they create for our business.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;What You&#39;ll Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the strategy and long-term plan for data supply: what we source, from whom, on what terms, and against what downstream demand&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Spend a lot of time in the market: source and qualify holders of proprietary data and own the funnel end-to-end (inbound and outbound). This will start as hands-on work, not oversight&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define and execute the qualification bar. Personally drive opportunity sourcing and qualification at each stage of the funnel, working with cross functional partners in Research, GTM, Delivery, and Legal&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Match opportunities to the right commercial structure and make the business case&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead negotiations end-to-end at the executive level, including business terms and partnering with Legal on critical terms such as sublicensing, etc.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage partnerships past signature through activation, development, sale, and renewal — act like an owner&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish the standards, operations, and metrics the function runs on — qualification gates, pricing framework, standard paper — then hire and develop a small team against them as the business scales&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as a key advisor to leadership with an opinionated view of the market: what&#39;s available, what it&#39;s worth, who else is bidding, and where we shouldn&#39;t play&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8+ years of experience leading commercial dealmaking roles — data or content licensing, strategic partnerships, in-licensing, or complex commercial contracting — with direct ownership of negotiations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience across meaningfully different business models or industries is critical. The economics of this market are still being invented, and we need someone who can blend experience, best practices, first principles, and market feedback&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working fluency in content licensing, IP, and data rights. You don&#39;t need to be a lawyer, but you need to know which terms determine whether a deal is worth doing, and to partner with Legal on where the key points sit&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven track record of managing partnerships past the signature, with results you can quantify: deals closed, value created, relationships you grew rather than inherited&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building and leading teams with high ownership and autonomy. You have taken an ambiguous mandate, built the pipeline, set the bar, and delivered impact&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Solid analytical and quantitative skills; comfortable building the simple model that tells us what an asset is worth to us and defending the assumptions in it&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Passion for unlocking new capabilities with modern AI is a must&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated interest and a strong point of view on the AI training and evaluation data market&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent written and verbal communication: you can tailor a message from IC to executive audience, and you&#39;re credible both in leadership discussions internally and as the first person a prospective partner&#39;s leadership team meets&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Actual compensation will be determined based on factors including skills, qualifications, experience, and geographic location.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Salary range(s) for this role&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$215,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$315,000 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Be Your Best at Snorkel&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Joining Snorkel AI means becoming part of a company that has market proven solutions, robust funding, and is scaling rapidly—offering a unique combination of stability and the excitement of high growth. As a member of our team, you’ll have meaningful opportunities to shape priorities and initiatives, influence key strategic decisions, and directly impact our ongoing success. Whether you’re looking to deepen your technical expertise, explore leadership opportunities, or learn new skills across multiple functions, you’re fully supported in building your career in an environment designed for growth, learning, and shared success.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Snorkel AI is proud to be an Equal Employment Opportunity employer and is committed to building a team that represents a variety of backgrounds, perspectives, and skills. Snorkel AI embraces diversity and provides equal employment opportunities to all employees and applicants for employment. Snorkel AI prohibits discrimination and harassment of any type on the basis of race, color, religion, age, sex, national origin, disability status, genetics, protected veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, or any other characteristic protected by federal, state, or local law. All employment is decided on the basis of qualifications, performance, merit, and business need.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;We will ensure that individuals with disabilities are provided reasonable accommodation to participate in the job application or interview process, to perform essential job functions, and to receive other benefits and privileges of employment. Please contact us to request accommodation.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;InMobi (Corporate)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;InMobi Group is a global technology company shaping the future of agentic commerce and advertising. Through its ecosystem of businesses — including InMobi Advertising and flagship consumer platform Glance — InMobi leverages data, machine learning, and generative AI to help brands reach audiences more precisely and consumers discover products more intuitively. Glance, which is pioneering new models of agentic commerce, is owned and operated by Glance InMobi Pte. Ltd., a non-consolidated subsidiary of InMobi Pte. Ltd.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;InMobi Advertising&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;InMobi Advertising, part of global technology company InMobi, is an agentic advertising platform helping brands and merchants achieve their business outcomes. Through its proprietary intelligence, AI-led solutions, and vast consumer reach — including flagship consumer platform Glance — InMobi Advertising delivers the omnichannel performance defining what&#39;s next in advertising and commerce. Glance is owned and operated by Glance InMobi Pte. Ltd., a non-consolidated subsidiary of InMobi Pte. Ltd. To learn more, visit advertising.inmobi.com.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Glance&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Glance is an intelligent shopping agent, redefining the commerce experience. Powered by proprietary agentic intelligence and generative AI, Glance delivers a hyper-personalized consumer experience across mobile and TV — shaping the new era of shopping. Glance is operated by Glance InMobi Pte. Ltd., a non-consolidated subsidiary of global technology leader InMobi, and is backed by Mithril Capital, Google and Jio Platforms. To learn more, visit glance.com.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What is the team like?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;NormalTextRun&quot;&gt;The GTM (Go-To-Market) Engineering team at &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;NormalTextRun SpellingErrorV2Themed&quot;&gt;InMobi&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;NormalTextRun&quot;&gt; builds and scales the systems that power revenue operations and customer engagement. The team owns a comprehensive Salesforce ecosystem—including Sales Cloud, Data Cloud, and &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;NormalTextRun SpellingErrorV2Themed&quot;&gt;Agentforce&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;NormalTextRun&quot;&gt;—along with Experience Cloud (Customer Community), enabling seamless workflows for Sales, Account Management, and Business teams. A key focus area is building intelligent agents and automations using &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;NormalTextRun SpellingErrorV2Themed&quot;&gt;Agentforce&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;NormalTextRun&quot;&gt;, integrated across Salesforce, Slack, and community platforms. These agents drive productivity, automate workflows, and enable real-time, context-aware actions for internal teams and customer-facing use cases. The team also &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;NormalTextRun&quot;&gt;leverages&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;NormalTextRun&quot;&gt; Slack as a collaboration and execution layer, tightly integrated with Salesforce to trigger workflows, surface insights, and enable faster decision-making. On the backend, the team develops and &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;NormalTextRun&quot;&gt;maintains&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;NormalTextRun&quot;&gt; a scalable middleware platform using Apache Camel and Java, powering event-driven &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;NormalTextRun&quot;&gt;integrations&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;NormalTextRun&quot;&gt; and reliable data exchange across systems. The architecture blends CRM, data platforms, agent-based automation, and distributed systems—focusing on extensibility, real-time processing, and high impact business outcomes. This is a high-impact engineering team &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;NormalTextRun&quot;&gt;operating&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;NormalTextRun&quot;&gt; at the intersection of CRM, AI-driven agents, integrations, and modern enterprise platforms.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;1&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Skillset:&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;span data-teams=&quot;true&quot;&gt;Agentforce (Agent Development),&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-teams=&quot;true&quot;&gt;Salesforce (Advanced), Apex, Lightning Web Components (LWC), Experience Cloud, Data Cloud, &amp;nbsp;Slack, CI/CD (Copado/GitHub), Event-Driven Architecture, Integration Patterns (Apache Camel), Java, Automation &amp;amp; Workflow Design, Performance Optimization, Python&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;2&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Role Overview&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;3&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;TextRun&quot; lang=&quot;EN-US&quot; data-contrast=&quot;none&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;NormalTextRun&quot;&gt;As an Architect/Staff &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;NormalTextRun ContextualSpellingAndGrammarErrorV2Themed&quot;&gt;Engineer I&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;NormalTextRun&quot;&gt; at &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;NormalTextRun SpellingErrorV2Themed&quot;&gt;InMobi&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;NormalTextRun&quot;&gt;, you will be a mentor, technical leader driving the design, development, and delivery of Agentic AI solutions on Salesforce platform. You will serve as the bridge between our CRM infrastructure and AI-driven product experiences &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;NormalTextRun&quot;&gt;-&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;NormalTextRun&quot;&gt; shaping how &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;NormalTextRun SpellingErrorV2Themed&quot;&gt;InMobi&#39;s&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;NormalTextRun&quot;&gt; go-to-market and revenue systems evolve and uplift in an era of autonomous workflows and intelligent automation. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;NormalTextRun&quot;&gt;You&#39;ll&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;NormalTextRun&quot;&gt; work closely with&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;NormalTextRun&quot;&gt; product team, RevOps, Data and product&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;NormalTextRun&quot;&gt; engineering to build scalable, distributed, enterprise-grade solutions that power&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;NormalTextRun SpellingErrorV2Themed&quot;&gt;InMobi&#39;s&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;NormalTextRun&quot;&gt; growth.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Salesforce platform engineering&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design, build, and deploy scalable Salesforce-centric solutions supporting InMobi&#39;s revenue and growth operations - including Agentforce / AI-driven orchestration, prompt templating, Data Cloud integration, complex Apex, LWC, and integration layers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design high-scale integrations with enterprise-grade architectures leveraging Platform Events, Change Data Capture (CDC), and REST/SOAP APIs to enable real-time data flows across the business.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build features enabling seamless integration between Salesforce structured/unstructured data and downstream AI agents for faster insights and decision-making.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deploy and monitor Salesforce-integrated products with an emphasis on agent observability, telemetry, and auditability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop best-in-class data health monitoring and context enrichment pipelines to ensure CRM data used by agents is reliable, governed, and audit-ready.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Agentic AI &amp;amp; intelligent automation&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead technical solutioning for full-lifecycle projects focused on how Salesforce will power autonomous workflows, co-pilots, and multi-agent systems - contributing to a &quot;data-first, agent-aware&quot; architecture strategy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with product management and business stakeholders to prioritize CRM data products that drive autonomous decision-making, context-rich recommendations, and discoverable data services for next-gen AI agents and LLM-based systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Distributed systems &amp;amp; backend&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Architect and scale distributed systems that interact with Salesforce for real-time data synchronization, leveraging Kafka, Spark, or similar streaming technologies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Write clean, testable, and high-performance backend middleware in Java that bridges CRM and cloud services at scale.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Engineering excellence&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Champion DevOps best practices including Salesforce DX, CI/CD pipelines (GitHub Actions), and automated testing frameworks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mentor engineering teams, set technical standards, and enforce code quality and best practices across squads.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to InMobi&#39;s platform reliability with a focus on fault tolerance, performance optimization, and scalability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you&#39;ll bring&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Required qualifications&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years of experience in enterprise software development with a focus on scalable, fault-tolerant, CRM-integrated architectures.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;2–3 years of hands-on experience with Agentforce, Data Cloud, and cloud platforms (GCP or Azure) and their connectivity to Salesforce.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep expertise in Salesforce architecture: Apex, LWC, Salesforce Shield, CRM data modelling, and high-volume data processing patterns.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven experience with advanced Salesforce integrations including Platform Events, CDC, and complex REST/SOAP API integrations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience writing optimized SOQL/SOSL and managing large datasets within Salesforce multi-tenant environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience writing clean, testable backend code in Java or Python for middleware services (Apache Camel, MuleSoft) bridging CRM and external cloud services.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mastery of Salesforce DX, CI/CD pipelines (GitHub Actions / Copado), and AI automated testing and deployment frameworks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of Salesforce data security including Data Mask, encryption, and governance in the context of agent auditability and compliance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Solid understanding of distributed systems and how tools like Kafka or Spark interact with Salesforce for real-time data synchronization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior experience at ad-tech or high-scale B2B SaaS companies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track record of building and delivering Agentic AI solutions for enterprise systems - including sophisticated Salesforce UIs and high-performance backend services.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with Salesforce Media Cloud, Order Management System (OMS), Revenue Cloud, or related platforms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with LLM evaluation, agent observability tooling, or RAG pipeline design.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;p3&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;s1&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The InMobi Culture&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At InMobi, culture isn’t a buzzword; it&#39;s an ethos woven by every InMobian, reflecting our diverse backgrounds and experiences.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We thrive on challenges and seize every opportunity for growth. Our core values — thinking big, being passionate, showing accountability, and taking ownership with freedom — guide us in every decision we make.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We believe in nurturing and investing in your development through continuous learning and career progression with our InMobi Live Your Potential program.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;InMobi is proud to be an Equal Employment Opportunity employer and is committed to providing reasonable accommodations to qualified individuals with disabilities throughout the hiring process and in the workplace.&lt;/p&gt;
